      "description": "`RunCommands` and `QueryFramesInto` unconditionally return `\"not implemented\"`, yet they replace the existing backend in active SQL paths. `sql.TablesList` calls `RunCommands`, so `NewSQLCommand` now rejects every nonempty SQL expression as invalid. The legacy path in `pkg/expr/nodes.go` still reaches this constructor through `UnmarshalSQLCommand`.\n\nThe new reader also rejects all SQL expressions: `enableSqlExpressions` in `pkg/expr/reader.go:194-200` returns `false` regardless of the feature flag. Consequently, neither parser path supports SQL expressions anymore, even when the feature is enabled.\n\nProvide a functioning replacement before removing the existing backend. If disabling SQL is intentional, consistently gate both parser paths and return an explicit feature-unavailable error rather than reporting valid SQL as invalid. Add active regression tests: the existing SQL parser and command tests are all skipped.",
